    "posts": {
      "inserted": [
        {
          "id": 53,
          "raw": "We’ve promoted you up another [trust level](https://blog.discourse.org/2018/06/understanding-discourse-trust-levels/)!\n\nAchieving Trust Level 2 means that you have read and actively participated enough to be considered a member of this community.\n\nAs an experienced user, you might appreciate [this list of handy tips and tricks](https://blog.discourse.org/2016/12/discourse-new-user-tips-and-tricks/).\n\nWe invite you to keep getting involved – we enjoy having you around.",
          "wiki": false,
          "reads": 1,
          "score": null,
          "cooked": "<p>We’ve promoted you up another <a href=\"https://blog.discourse.org/2018/06/understanding-discourse-trust-levels/\">trust level</a>!</p>\n<p>Achieving Trust Level 2 means that you have read and actively participated enough to be considered a member of this community.</p>\n<p>As an experienced user, you might appreciate <a href=\"https://blog.discourse.org/2016/12/discourse-new-user-tips-and-tricks/\">this list of handy tips and tricks</a>.</p>\n<p>We invite you to keep getting involved – we enjoy having you around.</p>",
